{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04TV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$G$", "MATH_0003": "$B$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$B$", "MATH_0006": "$G$", "MATH_0007": "$B$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5033e17d081b9098e662dda8f683dd360f033e5a533f8dc3e472949212177b1e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:25473959626117fc521618b79dbf74b40c4f94af2d65f86adafef60655ec7880", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe sometimes say ``let <MATH_0001> be a <MATH_0002>-principal homogeneous space over <MATH_0003>''\nto indicate that <MATH_0004> is an algebraic space over <MATH_0005> equipped with an\naction of <MATH_0006> which turns it into a principal homogeneous space over <MATH_0007>.\nNext we show that this agrees with the notation introduced earlier\nwhen both apply.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3dbe3e3c1b8c7daf2fa501116013bdd729a30e84fa9893bd1756071906cb01e7", "unit_id": "tag:04TV:prose-0003"}
